<p><strong>To start a barbershop in Nepal, set your services and prices, schedule your barbers, plan for both walk-ins and appointments, and record every payment from the first day. Check registration, licence and tax rules with the relevant Nepali authorities.</strong></p>
<p>This is an operations guide, not legal or tax advice. Confirm registration, licence, health and tax rules with the relevant authorities and your accountant.</p>
<h2>1. Keep the service list short</h2>
<p>Haircut, beard trim, shave, colour and a few combinations are enough to begin. Give each a realistic time, because that time decides how many clients one barber can serve.</p>
<h2>2. Plan the barbers' chairs and shifts</h2>
<p>Your chairs and barbers limit your revenue. Plan shifts and breaks, and track who did which service. See <a href="/features/staff-management/">staff management</a>.</p>
<h2>3. Handle walk-ins and appointments together</h2>
<p>Walk-ins are the core of many shops, but they collide with booked clients at busy hours. Read <a href="/blog/walk-in-queue-management-salon-barbershop-nepal/">how to manage a walk-in queue</a> and <a href="/blog/barbershop-booking-app-nepal/">how a barbershop booking app works</a>.</p>
<h2>4. Let regulars book their own barber</h2>
<p>Regulars ask for a specific barber. <a href="/features/booking/">Online booking</a> lets them choose the barber and a free time without a call.</p>
<h2>5. Record every payment</h2>
<p>Cash, card and online payments should all be recorded as they are taken. See <a href="/features/payment-tracking/">payment tracking</a>.</p>
<h2>6. Decide how barbers are paid</h2>
<p>Fixed salary, commission or both? Whichever you pick, record it before the first month ends. See <a href="/features/payroll/">payroll</a> and <a href="/blog/therapist-commission-payroll-nepal/">how commission and payroll work</a>.</p>
<h2>7. Plan for a second shop</h2>
<p>Choose software that scales. See <a href="/solutions/barbershop/">Zennly for barbershops</a>, or <a href="#try-free" data-trial-open>try the free Zennly demo</a>.</p>
